<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Skårasalen from Kvistadsætra — Kvistadsætra–Skårasalen normal dry snow-free return [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From Kvistadsætra above Hjørundfjord, follow the road to the Skårasalen turn and the intermittent path up the gully’s left side. Continue through the passage between Blåhornet and Skårasalen, cross the plateau toward the Lille Skårasalen saddle and climb loose stones to the main summit. Return the same way. Plan roughly 6.8 km and five hours; climbing figures are approximate. The path is indistinct in places, with very steep ground and loose upper stones. Use dry, snow-free conditions only, check current local advice and turn back if footing or exposure exceeds your ability.

Route geometry: © Kartverket — https://www.kartverket.no/; N50 Kartdata Samferdsel. CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Dataset/source: https://www.geonorge.no/geonetwork/srv/api/records/ea192681-d039-42ec-b1bc-f3ce04c189ac/formatters/xml. Whole original Ørsta source: https://nedlasting.geonorge.no/geonorge/Basisdata/N50Kartdata/GML/Basisdata_1520_Orsta_25832_N50Kartdata_GML.zip. Changes: original EPSG:25832 coordinates transformed to WGS84; three complete source records ordered at two literal junctions and retraced for the return; display geometry retains the full original source-vertex sequence under the existing configured display budget. No elevation assigned. Descriptive planning geometry, not navigation-grade.

